gue","start":1795006257.0,"end":1795022376.0,"status":"stopped","start_text":"2026-11-18 13:50","end_text":"2026-11-18 18:19"}],"z1":[{"stage":"self-play","start":1795003904.0,"end":1795006253.0,"status":"passed","start_text":"2026-11-18 13:11","end_text":"2026-11-18 13:50"},{"stage":"bots","start":1795006253.0,"end":1795006257.0,"status":"passed","start_text":"2026-11-18 13:50","end_text":"2026-11-18 13:50"},{"stage":"league","start":1795006257.0,"end":1795024693.0,"status":"stopped","start_text":"2026-11-18 13:50","end_text":"2026-11-18 18:58"}],"z2":[{"stage":"self-play","start":1795023377.0,"end":1795028920.0,"status":"stopped","start_text":"2026-11-18 18:36","end_text":"2026-11-18 20:08"}],"z1h":[{"stage":"self-play","start":1795003904.0,"end":1795006253.0,"status":"passed","start_text":"2026-11-18 13:11","end_text":"2026-11-18 13:50"},{"stage":"bots","start":1795006253.0,"end":1795006257.0,"status":"passed","start_text":"2026-11-18 13:50","end_text":"2026-11-18 13:50"},{"stage":"league","start":1795006257.0,"end":1795026896.0,"status":"stopped","start_text":"2026-11-18 13:50","end_text":"2026-11-18 19:34"}],"z3":[{"stage":"self-play","start":1795029137.0,"end":1795031493.0,"status":"stopped","start_text":"2026-11-18 20:12","end_text":"2026-11-18 20:51"}]},"decisions":[{"t":"2026-11-18 20:12:01","kind":"decision","title":"z3: from zero with the helper inputs","text":"The helper inputs gave z1h +4 to +6 points against rl-v1 and az-v1 within 30 iterations. z3 tests them from the start: random weights, exactly z1's settings (1,500 games per iteration, same stages), only the 413 inputs instead of 298, so every iteration compares with z1.","rejected":"Keeping z2 (its question is answered); more exploration in z3 (it did not change the style)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 18:58:06","kind":"decision","title":"Helper inputs: what the next hand brings, and what a card would change","text":"115 new inputs computed exactly from what the player knows (the draw pile's contents, then the reshuffle): the next hand's expected coins, chances of $3/$5/$6/$8, expected action cards, +Actions, +Buys, +Cards, expected VP gain (best Victory card it can afford) and VP after it; the deck's coins/actions/+Actions/+Buys/+Cards per 5 cards; and for every card, how one more copy changes coins, +Actions and +Buys per 5 cards. Added to z1 at iteration 1095 with zero weights (same play, checked on 20 games) as run z1h; z1 goes on unchanged as the comparison.","rejected":"Learning these from the raw counts (the net has the counts but must learn division and hypergeometric odds); Monte Carlo estimates (noisy, and hard to reproduce bit-exactly in the browser)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 18:36:09","kind":"decision","title":"z2: a second run from zero, exploring from the start","text":"z1's style locked in by iteration ~250 and nothing applied later (learning rate, entropy, kingdom curriculum) changed it. z2 starts from random weights again with an entropy bonus of 0.05 falling to 0.01 over 600 iterations (z1: 0.01 throughout; its entropy fell from 1.37 to 0.3 in 40 iterations) and the kingdom curriculum (30% of games without the attack and Gardens cards) from iteration 1. Same stages, same evaluation.","rejected":"Only waiting for z1 to drift (rl-v1 needed ~2,000 league iterations); restarting z1 itself (it is the baseline)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"Start from random weights, no imitation","text":"rl-v2 tests whether the GA genome is a head start or a ceiling: same network, inputs and PPO as rl-v1, only the start changes. Self-play first, then the bots, then every earlier model.","rejected":"Imitation first (that is rl-v1); a new architecture (would mix two changes into one comparison)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"Stage 1 ends on a plateau, not a score","text":"The first start ended self-play after 12 iterations, when it beat the bots 50% of the time. Self-play is the point of the project, so stage 1 now runs until the score against the GA genome has not improved for 60 iterations (at most 400): it shows how far self-play gets alone.","rejected":"A fixed bots threshold (ended the stage after 3 minutes); a fixed iteration count (could stop while it is still learning, or waste hours on a plateau)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"1,500 games per iteration","text":"Random players make long games with ~210 decisions each; 3,000 of them (rl-v1's setting) ran the 8 GB laptop out of memory. 1,500 fit with room for the evaluation.","rejected":"Keeping 3,000 with float16 features (a change to the shared code that rl-v1 does not have)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"Same evaluation games as rl-v1","text":"The per-iteration evaluation and the goal checks use rl-v1's and az-v1's seeds, so every number compares directly with them. A new confirmation seed is kept for the end.","rejected":"New evaluation seeds (no direct comparison)."}],"reports":[],"strip":{"alive":false,"run":"z1h","stage":"3","goal_text":"82.8%","stages_text":"2 of 3 stages passed","best_text":"75.1%","verified_text":"74.0%","verified_sub":"z1h iteration 1125, n=1000"}}